- Get configuration, Get fleet, List fleets, and the other endpoints that return a config or fleet now list the configuration profiles, scripts, setup experience assets, and VPP token assignments saved in Fleet, whether they were added via YAML, the UI, or the API. Items are listed by name instead of their YAML path or URL, and a list is left out of the response when the user's role can't view it. Update configuration and applying fleet specs now ignore a `null` bootstrap package or setup assistant (including an empty key in a `fleetctl apply` file) instead of deleting it; send `""` to delete it.
